tg wrote:
> What do you generally do - make a wish right away or use it as a
> permanent light source?

A single magic lamp is my permanent light source, and I take it with
me until Astral.

Mostly.

Exceptions to that are in games where I really *really* lack something
important; levitation, any means to resist polytraps, bag of holding,
reflection. But I delay that decision as long as _safely_ possible. For
example, I don't wish for reflection or a bag if I haven't done Sokoban
yet. I don't wish for better armor if I don't mind polytraps because I
have spare body armor and spare cloaks. I don't wish for dragon armor
as long as I've not checked the throne rooms, Ludios, and the Castle.
If there's any major spellcaster and I haven't yet got MR then I'd try
to wish for GDSM.

