That's quite sufficient for some time. And you may (or may not) find
another magic lamp later if you decide to spend the (only) one you have.

> - item that i wish for may improve my chance of survival

Hmm, I am ambivalent about that point; it's too easily said. But you never
know what you will need to survive! That's why above I said that I delay
the decision until I know what's best to increase the survival probability.
So it actually depends on where you are, what you've discovered so far,
what you have (intrinsic and inventory), and it depends on your experience
how to handle situations where you not yet have the optimum means to solve
it. But remember, many problematic situations can be foreseen and you can
still retreat and wish for what you need at that time.

